    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **255 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for owners. When a request includes `birthDate` (ISO date), the response now returns `ageBand` computed against the owner's `registrationDate`: `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+); absent when no `birthDate` was supplied.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (optional, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema, and a read-only `ageBand` string to the `Owner` response schema. These regenerate the DTOs with the new fields.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, column `birth_date`) with getter/setter, so the value survives create \u2192 DB \u2192 GET.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `ageBand(owner)` helper and mapped it onto `toOwnerDto`. It uses `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` and returns null when either date is missing. `birthDate` itself maps automatically by name in both directions (request\u2192entity, entity\u2192response).\n\n4. **DB schema** (`h2`, `hsqldb`, `mysql`, `postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column.\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** (the test DB) \u2014 the seed owners use positional `INSERT ... VALUES`, so I extended each of the 10 rows with a trailing `NULL` to match the new column count. (h2/postgres seeds use explicit column lists and needed no change.)\n\nThe flow needs no new OfficeFloor function: `BuildOwner` already maps the request body into the entity (now carrying `birthDate`), and the existing responder/GET pipeline derives `ageBand` through the mapper. The provided acceptance test `coreDerivesAgeBand` (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`) passes, along with all existing tests.",
